################ ZT-053-a-root-whose-signature-algorithm-the-parser
== the two certificates
   both are publicly trusted roots, both self-signed, both RSASSA-PSS,
   and both have subject == issuer. They differ in one field.
   ZT-053-pss-root-absent-hash-params.pem         D-TRUST Root CA 1 2017
   ZT-053-control-pss-root-null-hash-params.pem   Staat der Nederlanden - G4 Root Publ G-SMIME - 2024

== the field: the hashAlgorithm inside RSASSA-PSS-params
   ZT-053-pss-root-absent-hash-params.pem
         16:d=2  hl=2 l=   9 prim: OBJECT            :rsassaPss
         27:d=2  hl=2 l=  48 cons: SEQUENCE          
         29:d=3  hl=2 l=  13 cons: cont [ 0 ]        
         31:d=4  hl=2 l=  11 cons: SEQUENCE          
   ZT-053-control-pss-root-null-hash-params.pem
         33:d=2  hl=2 l=   9 prim: OBJECT            :rsassaPss
         44:d=2  hl=2 l=  52 cons: SEQUENCE          
         46:d=3  hl=2 l=  15 cons: cont [ 0 ]        
         48:d=4  hl=2 l=  13 cons: SEQUENCE          
   The [0] hashAlgorithm holds 13 octets in the first and 15 in the
   second: the same id-sha512 OBJECT IDENTIFIER, plus a two-octet
   NULL (05 00). That NULL is the whole difference between the two
   certificates as far as this defect is concerned.

== the role each is given, by the lints that only a ROOT can be judged by
   e_root_ca_key_usage_present                                    absent=NA   NULL=pass
   e_root_ca_key_usage_must_be_critical                           absent=NA   NULL=pass
   e_root_ca_extended_key_usage_present                           absent=NA   NULL=pass
   w_root_ca_contains_cert_policy                                 absent=NA   NULL=pass
   w_root_ca_basic_constraints_path_len_constraint_field_present  absent=NA   NULL=pass

== and by the lints only a SUBORDINATE CA can be judged by
   e_sub_ca_certificate_policies_missing                          absent=error NULL=NA
   e_sub_ca_aia_missing                                           absent=error NULL=NA
   e_sub_ca_crl_distribution_points_missing                       absent=pass NULL=NA
   n_sub_ca_eku_missing                                           absent=info NULL=NA
   w_sub_ca_aia_does_not_contain_issuing_ca_url                   absent=warn NULL=NA

== a third consequence of the same unrecognised algorithm
   subject: {"e_signature_algorithm_not_supported":{"result":"error"}}
   control: {"e_signature_algorithm_not_supported":{"result":"warn"}}
   Both are SHA-512 RSASSA-PSS. The recognised one warns, which is what
   zlint means to say about PSS; the unrecognised one errors, because the
   lint reads c.SignatureAlgorithm and finds UnknownSignatureAlgorithm.

observed  D-TRUST Root CA 1 2017 is judged as a subordinate CA: it is
          reported for a missing certificatePolicies and a missing AIA,
          neither of which a root must carry, and the five root-profile
          lints never run on it at all.
correct   the role is a property of the certificate, not of whether this
          parser could check its signature. Either give IsRootCA a
          name-equality path when the signature cannot be checked, or
          accept absent hashAlgorithm parameters as RFC 4055 s2.1
          requires -- the one-line form is to use the same condition the
          unexported sibling in the same file already uses.

